
# InventoryManagementAPI

A full-featured inventory management REST API built with ASP.NET Core and Entity Framework Core, following professional software architecture patterns.

## What It Does

Manages products and categories stored in a SQL Server database. Implements the Repository Pattern for clean separation of concerns, exposes a complete CRUD API documented with Swagger, and includes both unit and integration tests.

## Tech Stack

- ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8)
- Entity Framework Core 8.0 (Code-First)
- SQL Server (LocalDB)
- Swagger / OpenAPI
- xUnit 2.9.3 (unit testing)
- Moq (mocking)
- FluentAssertions (integration testing)

## Architecture

```
InventoryManagementAPI/
├── Controllers/        # ProductController — REST endpoints
├── Data/               # ApplicationDbContext — EF Core configuration
├── Models/             # Product, Category — domain entities
├── Repositories/       # IProductRepository, ProductRepository — data access layer
├── appsettings.json    # Database connection string
└── Program.cs          # Service registration and middleware pipeline

InventoryManagementAPI.Tests/
└── ProductControllerTests.cs   # Unit tests with Moq

InventoryManagementAPI.IntegrationTests/
└── ProductIntegrationTests.cs  # Integration tests with in-memory DB
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/product` | Get all products (with category) |
| GET | `/api/product/{id}` | Get product by ID |
| POST | `/api/product` | Create a new product |
| PUT | `/api/product/{id}` | Update a product |
| DELETE | `/api/product/{id}` | Delete a product |

## How to Run

**Prerequisites:** Visual Studio 2022, .NET 8 SDK, SQL Server LocalDB

1. Open the solution in Visual Studio 2022
2. Open Package Manager Console and install dependencies:
   ```
   Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer -Version 8.0.0
   Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools -Version 8.0.0
   Install-Package Swashbuckle.AspNetCore
   ```
3. Run database migrations:
   ```
   Add-Migration InitialCreate
   Update-Database
   ```
4. Press **F5** to run — Swagger UI opens automatically at `https://localhost:{port}/swagger`

